	quest.362A953C6227E15D.title: "[017] (SOLVED) what's the name of that one show"
	quest.362D1C59144B8E23.quest_desc: [
		"&7> &rIn the furthest &5WESTERN&r reaches of the veil lie &5DREAM BUBBLES&r glubbed up by the &1OUTER GODS&r. Visiting these can net you important resources, like &3ASPECT SAPLINGS&r or &aFROGS&r. "
		""
		"&7> &rIt is imperative for sessions without a &8Hero of Space&r to travel to &5Dream Bubbles&r and retrieve frogs."
		""
		"&7> &rHow you travel to these bubbles is up to you, keeping in mind your &4inability to place or break blocks&r whilst in the &8Veil&r."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The bubbles allow the players of Sburb who have lost a life to continue dreaming. The reality constructed in the bubbles is a combination of the memories of everyone inside the bubble accessible to any who has learned the bubble's nature. "
		""
		"Additionally, living players, who have lost or become their dream selves, appear in the dream bubbles when they are asleep. It is in this fashion that the bubbles can be used as meeting places between the dead and the living; even those from alternate universes, such as the one that created yours, and doomed timelines can be found in a bubble."
	]
	quest.362D1C59144B8E23.title: "&1Bubble Up!"
	quest.36D09CCBDF8910E2.quest_desc: [
		"-- &#824d18unctuousUndertaking [UU]&r has created the memo CAN_WE_GET_THIS_OVER_WITH_I_WAS_BUSY --"
		"&#824d18UU: so ↺h, looks like yo↺ve finally entered. took yo↺ long eno↺gh ★_★ now we can finally get this over with"
		""
		"&#824d18UU: as yo↺ can probably tell, your land is all kind of messed ↺p. this is typical for Doom Players, mine was m↺ch of the same."
		""
		"&#824d18UU: ill be yo↺r g↺ide or whatever for the d↺ration of this. or atleast thats what shes telling me to do."
		"-- &#824d18UU&r Closed Memo --"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&2“Those bound to the aspect of Doom are fate's chosen sufferers. It may not sound like an overly pleasant aspect to be aligned with, but it does come along with great wisdom and empathy. The Doom-bound understand that misery loves company, and they are ready and willing to provide said company. The Doom-bound won't fix you; they aren't healers. They are commiserators, aware that sometimes the only thing you can do for a person is let them know that they are not alone in their suffering. They are not the advice friend-they're the friend you go to when you need to vent about a rough day at work. They are not necessarily noble martyrs, either-the Doom-bound can become quite irate about their lot. At their best they are wise, kind, and non-judgemental. At their worst, bitter, resentful, and fatalistic.”"
		"&2— The Extended Zodiac"
	]
	quest.36D09CCBDF8910E2.title: "&#824d18Fate's Chosen Sufferer"
	quest.36E88C5CB0024F28.quest_desc: [
		"&#a64d9aRG: by now youve probably encounTered the lisT. or maybe youve even compleTed iT. your Timeline is all messed up, so iTs hard To Tell."
		""
		"&#a64d9aRG: kill The residenTs of this land in ThaT order or iT doesnT counT."
